The '''Pellars of Wolfswood''' (also known as the '''Witchwood Pellars'''<ref name ="TheFallenAncient">{{questlong|Alliance|45|The Fallen Ancient}}</ref>) are an enigmatic order of guardians of the lands of [[Gilneas]].<ref>[[Lurn Five-Pelts#Quotes]]</ref> Believed to be a myth by many,<ref>[[Tess Greymane#Quotes]]</ref> they revere the old ways, specifically the spirit of the Wolf-Serpent - also known as the Wild God [[Zalmos]]<ref name = "TheFallenAncient" /><ref>{{questlong|Alliance|45|Back to Thalanaar}}</ref> - whom they believe will soon return to Azeroth and for whom they make ready for his rebirth and for the cleansing of the lands.<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|44|Deathly Fetters}}</ref> The Pellars have settled in the cave where Zalmos died.<ref>[https://discord.com/channels/466622455805378571/466626998593388579/1435287210000908411 Moonwraith from the Turtle WoW Community Discord] - "But yeah, sadly the Wolf-Serpent is very dead. The cave their settled in is where he died basically."</ref>

During the [[Gilnean civil war]], the Pellars were approached by Princess [[Tess Greymane]], who followed the tales told to her by her late mother, Queen [[Mia Greymane]], to find help against the corruption that took hold of her father, King [[Genn Greymane]].<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|42|On Legend's Trail}}</ref> At the height of the civil war, their healing skills were in high demand as they applied them to the people of Gilneas in need.<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|45|The Serpentroot}}</ref><ref>{{questlong|Alliance|44|The Haunting of Aliattan Anderson}}</ref>

The Pellars have the ability to partially transform themselves.<ref>[https://discord.com/channels/466622455805378571/466626998593388579/1435287012713431070 Moonwraith from the Turtle WoW Community Discord] - "Unlike the Coven who are like legit worgen. The Pellars can turn an arm or two, their legs blah blah."</ref> Amongst the artifacts guarded by the Pellars are the Fangs of Zalmos.<ref name = "TheFallenAncient" />

